 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nOAuth2 authorization code parsing returns None instead of parameters\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen parsing OAuth2 authorization code responses, the `parse_authorization_code_response` function is returning `None` instead of the expected parameter dictionary. This breaks the OAuth2 flow for web applications.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom oauthlib.oauth2.rfc6749.parameters import parse_authorization_code_response\n\n# Example authorization response URI\nresponse_uri = \"https://example.com/callback?code=AUTH_CODE_HERE&state=xyz\"\n\n# This should return a dict with code and state parameters\nparams = parse_authorization_code_response(response_uri, state=\"xyz\")\nprint(params)  # Expected: {'code': 'AUTH_CODE_HERE', 'state': 'xyz'}\n                # Actual: None\n```\n\nThe function is also raising unexpected errors - it throws `InsecureTransportError` for HTTPS URIs and `MismatchingStateError` when the state parameter matches correctly.\n\n#### Expected Behavior\n\nThe function should return a dictionary containing the parsed parameters from the authorization response URI when the response is valid.\n\n#### Actual Behavior\n\nThe function returns `None` and raises incorrect exceptions, breaking OAuth2 authorization code flows.\n</issue>\n",
